<div class="help-panel"><h2>Start with the catalog</h2><p>Open Movies, People, or Songs. Use the table’s search box or column filters, then choose <strong>View</strong> to open a record. OMDB searches the records already stored here; it does not automatically download missing films or credits.</p><div class="page-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="movies.php">Browse movies</a><a class="btn btn-default" href="advance_movie_search.php">Find movies</a></div></div>
<section class="help-section" id="browse"><h2>Browse, filter, and explore</h2><ul><li><strong>Movies:</strong> titles, release year, cast, directors, songs, and additional movie information.</li><li><strong>People:</strong> stage names, profile details, and movie or song credits.</li><li><strong>Songs:</strong> titles, lyrics, themes, and related credits.</li><li>Use <strong>Filter results</strong> to search the whole table. Column filters narrow one field. Clear the text to show all records again.</li><li>Use <strong>Show rows</strong> and <strong>Previous / Next</strong> to move through long lists. A table with no matches means its filters need adjusting.</li><li>After signing in, <strong>Reports</strong> lets you explore movies by year and contributor. <strong>Games</strong> includes base characters, anagrams, and Movie in Movies.</li></ul></section>
<section class="help-section" id="search-help"><h2>Search by cast and director together</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="advance_movie_search.php">Find movies</a> from Search.</li><li>Enter a name under <strong>Cast member</strong> and another under <strong>Director</strong>. You can use a stage name, full name, or part of a name.</li><li>Optionally add a movie title or open <strong>More credit filters</strong> for lead actor, lead actress, producer, or music director.</li><li>Choose <strong>Find movies</strong>. Every filled filter must match the same movie.</li></ol><p>The main search box also accepts <code>movies with Brad Pitt directed by Steven Spielberg</code>. This opens the cast and director filters. Both names and their matching credits must already be stored in OMDB; this example may return no results in your catalog.</p><p>Other text in the main search box searches movie titles, people, and songs. Use the Songs or People search categories for their dedicated filters. Use <strong>Clear filters</strong> to start over. Movie filter URLs can be bookmarked or shared.</p></section>
<section class="help-section" id="accounts"><h2>Accounts and permissions</h2><p>Guests can browse the public catalog. Sign in with the account provided by your administrator for member features such as Reports.</p><p><strong>Members</strong> browse and search. <strong>Administrators</strong> also create, edit, delete, import, and manage relationships. Admin controls are shown only to administrators. If a record needs correcting, ask your administrator.</p><p>Use <strong>Sign out</strong> when finished on a shared computer. If your account is missing or you cannot sign in, contact your administrator. Never put account passwords into source files or shared reports.</p></section>
<section class="help-section" id="small-screens"><h2>Phones, tablets, and smaller windows</h2><p>Use <strong>Menu</strong> to open the main navigation on smaller screens. Search categories and section links wrap below the header. Forms stack vertically to stay readable.</p><p>Wide tables scroll sideways within their own area. When the scroll hint appears, swipe across the table or focus the table region and use the arrow keys. Page controls and form buttons stay at least large enough for a touch target.</p></section>
<section class="help-section" id="troubleshooting"><h2>Messages and troubleshooting</h2><ul><li><strong>No matches:</strong> check spelling, try part of a name, or clear a filter. Missing people or credits cannot appear in results.</li><li><strong>Please check these details:</strong> read the highlighted message, correct the named field, and save again. Required fields and character limits are shown on the main forms.</li><li><strong>Changes saved / Record created:</strong> the operation completed. Confirm the record in its catalog or detail page.</li><li><strong>Access unavailable:</strong> sign in with the appropriate account. A member account cannot make database changes, including through a saved admin link.</li><li><strong>Expired form:</strong> reload the form and try again. A form from an older sign-in session may need refreshing.</li><li><strong>Records could not be loaded:</strong> reload the page. If the problem continues, tell your administrator which page you were using; technical errors are kept out of the page.</li></ul></section>
